{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/957123-favorite-pantheon","id":957123,"title":"Favorite Pantheon?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-24T12:51:07-07:00","id":957123,"title":"Favorite Pantheon?","content":"I think it's safe to assume that everyone here is a mythology nerd of one stripe or another, and while the field is inevitably broad there has to be one mythology that grabs you more than the rest. Which are you most excited for, going into the new edition of Scion?<br /> <br /> (For reference: the Greco-Roman, Egyptian, Norse, Hindu, Chinese, Japanese, Algonquian, Yoruba, Aztec, and Irish gods are confirmed for Hero, with the Persian, Vodoun, Mayan, Gaulish, Inuit, Polynesian, Mesopotamian, and Aboriginal Australian pantheons all mentioned in some degree for later products.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T14:05:15-07:00","id":957177,"title":"","content":"And the Welsh pantheon, but I really want to do a big book for them. <b>Scion: The Once and Future King</b> is my working title, although one writer suggested <b>Scion: Cwm and Get It</b>.<br /> <br /> My favorite is the Irish pantheon, surprising nobody.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T14:10:23-07:00","id":957178,"title":"","content":"I have a past partiality to the Norse and Greeks. While I still find them interesting, the myths of Japan currently hold the top spot although I am suitably intrigued by the roster of pantheons presented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T14:57:32-07:00","id":957205,"title":"","content":"Hands down the Irish. Scion 1E got me into them back in Grade 10, and now I'm writing my Master's Application to go and do a Celtic Studies program in 2017. They are <i>so</i> great, they break molds, and defy things. The Pantheon never bothered to make the world! That is, apparently, not relevant! We never learn the ancient family lines of the Pantheon, not important! The story is not one of the Gods, it is the story of Ireland, and everyone clamoring to take, and hold the precious gem of a land. <br /> <br /> The Gods <i>die</i>! Not by each other, <i>Mortals</i> show up and kick everyone's teeth in. Sure, it's a hard fought battle and the Tuatha were already badly weakened from the usurpation of Bres, but the <i>Mortals</i> killed the divine. But, the Mortals, are they mortal? They can do <i>things</i>, strange, and powerful, entirely partitioned from Divinity. The Intoxication of the Ulstermen has droves, and droves of these Heroes. I'll leave you with my favorite passage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Intoxication of the Ulstermen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I saw a young lad, almost a child, bound and fettered. Three chains round each leg and a chain round each arm; three chains round his neck and seven Men holding each chain, seventy-seven men in all. He turned strongly and powerfully and overthrew the sevenry-seven men, dealing with them as lightly and swiftly as he would have dealt with puffballs. When he perceived the smell of his enemies, when he strick the head of a man against a projecting clod, or against a rock of stone, then that man would say &quot;it is not for valor or glory that this trick is preformed, but by reason of the food and drink in the fort.&quot; the lad blushed and fell silent and went about with them until the same wave of savagery overcame him.'<br /> <br /> 'Destructive and interactable that description, indeed, said Medb. 'Destructive and interactable the one described,' said Cu Rui. 'He is the son of three champions of whom I spoke a short while ago: Uma son of Remanfissech, Errge Echbel, and Celtchair son of Uthechar. That many of the host are needed to guard him and to restrain his valor when he goes to the land of his enemies. Uanchend Arritech he, and he is only eleven years old, and never has consumed a portion of food that he did not offer to everyone in the house.'&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/957123-favorite-pantheon?p=957177#post957177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">, although one writer suggested <b>Scion: Cwm and Get It</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>That</i> is brilliant. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T16:47:36-07:00","id":957268,"title":"","content":"I was a big fan of Greek mythology back in school, and it's the pantheon I'm most familiarized with. But in retrospect, the Greco-Romans were a bunch of self centered ass holes who demanded impossible standards from their worshipers.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Aspire to greatness, or be cast into limbo for eternity.&quot;would certainly motivate your society, but not everybody is so gifted.<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------<br /> <br /> I'd have to say my new favorite is probably the Egyptian pantheon. Due in large part to what I believe is a distinct lack of Hell. If you were a bad person, your soul just ceased to exist. Which sounds a lot better than the eternal punishment the other pantheons have concocted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T17:42:24-07:00","id":957289,"title":"","content":"The one I'm most familiar with is the Greco-Roman pantheon, so it beats out the others when it comes to imagining Scion. I'm also a big fan of the God of War series, so to me, the fact that the gods are jerks just means that a story that includes them can logically lead to a theomachy, so.<br /> <br /> My second favorite are the Norse - gotta love those fair-haired lunatics! Let's go fight some frost giants!<br /> <br /> Third favorite is the Netjer - thanks to a few certain modern pulp movies, when I think two-fisted tales of questing for lost relics, Ancient Egypt is the place to go.<br /> <br /> I would like to get to know all of them better, but the ones I'm most looking forward to learning more about are the Tuatha De Danaan and Welsh pantheons. I'm told I'm of Scotch-Irish descent, so I'd be learning about my ancestral British Isles culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 08-24-2016, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T18:32:34-07:00","id":957308,"title":"","content":"The Egyptians, the Norse, and the Aztecs, in that order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T19:15:23-07:00","id":957333,"title":"","content":"1.) The Norse: They're the gods of my ancestors. They'll always have that special place in my heart. I love how they fight against Fate itself. The BALLS on those guys and gals, right? Plus, Viking culture is just fun. They were a people ahead of their time in a lot of ways. <br /> <br /> 2.) The Theoi: They were my first mythological love. Yeah, they're assholes, but they at least manage to be EPIC assholes. If you're going to be something, you may as well do it with gusto!<br /> <br /> 3.) The Annuna: They're just like the Theoi--they go big in everything they do--plus, they built the oldest civilization in human record. Big props.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T23:56:02-07:00","id":958085,"title":"","content":"I know the most about the Greco-Roman, Mesopotamian and Norse pantheons, but that doesn't necessarily make any of them my favourites.<br /> <br /> Hmm... I'm generally a fan of the more bizzare, non-traditional type pantheons, and ever since I started researching m heritage I've developed a fondness for the Celtic pantheons, so... the Tuatha, I suppose. Maybe the Welsh or the Gaulish pantheons, once I get a good look at 'em.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T01:19:14-07:00","id":958105,"title":"","content":"1) \u00d2r\u00ec\u1e63\u00e0, 2) Loa, 3) Sh\u00e9n","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T01:48:43-07:00","id":958115,"title":"","content":"I just can't pick, it can't be done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T08:45:31-07:00","id":958247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/957123-favorite-pantheon?p=957205#post957205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>That</i> is brilliant.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It's not. It's kinda weird and almost certainly insulting.<br /> <br /> If it's a verb, which it is by context, &quot;Cwm and Get It&quot; is, then it's effectively &quot;Bend Over and Get It&quot;.<br /> <br /> If it's a noun, it makes no sense. &quot;Valley and Get It&quot;<br /> <br /> Why not call the Tuatha De &quot;Island and Getting Drunk&quot;? Is that cool? Not really.<br /> <br /> Especially since there are almost certainly more appropriate things they could be called. Like, say, Tylweth, which would be analogous to the meaning of Tuatha in Gaelic and has some precedent (the Tylwyth Teg or &quot;Fair Folk&quot; who have the same weird interconnected relationship to the hero/gods of the Mabinogion as the sidhe do to the Tuatha De), or considering the two dominant families, perhaps Dau Tylwythau<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 08-26-2016, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T18:22:54-07:00","id":958539,"title":"","content":"Unless there's some sort of stereoype about Welsh people and rape that I'm unaware of, I don't really see how it's insulting. I think it's just some wordplay.<br /> <br /> I do agree, however, that there are probably better names for the Welsh supplement book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T20:07:18-07:00","id":958579,"title":"","content":"I think naming any pantheon book, essentially, a play on, &quot;Bend Over and Take It&quot;, is pretty insulting to any target group, extant or extinct, if intentional. Cancel, that, not &quot;pretty insulting&quot;, as a not-so-borderline rape innuendo, it's pretty abhorrent. <br /> <br /> If accidental, then is is something to be assiduously avoided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T20:26:21-07:00","id":958588,"title":"","content":"Since Cwm is pronounced, &quot;Coom&quot; from what I could see, I read it as a play of words around &quot;Come and Get It.&quot; I don't think Neall or his authors would be making a rape joke at all. And, on top of that, it didn't seem like a serious answer at all, just a pun for the title.<br /> <br /> Neall and his team look to be putting a lot of work into making things culturally appropriate, giving the Netjer their real names for example as he's talked about in the Ask Neall thread. Pretty sure we can make a safe assumption that it's a joke suggestion, and a pronunciation pun rather than a rape joke. I mean, like, even if some strike of utter lunacy hit the dev team, I would hope that titling a publication as a rape joke wouldn't get past a single editor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":".  Still can't spell. 08-26-2016, 11:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T20:56:28-07:00","id":958594,"title":"","content":"Doesn't matter. Intent is important but not dispositive. That's what &quot;negligence&quot; is. Doing something wrong or inappropriate out of ignorance or lack of attention.<br /> <br /> I doubt the intent to lampoon the Welsh language with the rip-roaring (and somewhat juvenile) fun of replacing a word in an English phrase with a word that sounds similar but means completely different things wasn''t malicious. I don't think it was well-advised to begin with. It was a silly attempt at something like a stab at a cross-language pun. But, if it ended up being a fart joke at the expense of the Welsh, it would still be a pretty crappy thing to do. This can definitely come across more than a bit worse than that. I knew EXACTLY what the intent was, but thought it made no sense as my immediate impression was seeing &quot;cwm&quot; as &quot;valley&quot; and then doing a double-take and re-reading it as a verb. <br /> <br /> Apparently, absent any comments to the contrary, this name DID get by Neal and his team as is. He threw it out there as an offhand joke. Things as bad, and worse, have gotten by editors of White Wolf games in the past. Great chance to catch it now and kill it dead, dead, dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T00:30:49-07:00","id":958627,"title":"","content":"Personally, my favorite would be the Theoi. It isn't that the other pantheons aren't interesting as well. My wife and I had a lot of fun with games centered around the Aesir and the Tuatha, as well. Games centered around the Theoi have always been a guilty (and debatably blasphemous) pleasure, though, and they are always first in my heart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T05:56:23-07:00","id":958703,"title":"","content":"Like most people, I know more of Greek mythology than any others. As a Macanese, I was able to watch and listen to stories that surround Sunwukong and his journey to the west (if you like Stephen Chow, Xiyouqi is really a movie to watch!!! It's entertaining and culturally speaking... well I still learned a lot from it hehe<br /> <br /> Um... the top 3 would be:<br /> <br /> 1) Greek<br /> 2) Chinese<br /> 3) Japanese<br /> <br /> But Aztec, Mesopotamian and Mayan could be very interesting... I just need to know more about them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1837,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","user":"Wickedgrail","date":". 08-28-2016, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T16:34:14-07:00","id":958951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/957123-favorite-pantheon?p=958594#post958594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt the intent to lampoon the Welsh language with the rip-roaring (and somewhat juvenile) fun of replacing a word in an English phrase with a word that sounds similar but means completely different things wasn''t malicious. I don't think it was well-advised to begin with. It was a silly attempt at something like a stab at a cross-language pun. But, if it ended up being a fart joke at the expense of the Welsh, it would still be a pretty crappy thing to do. This can definitely come across more than a bit worse than that. I knew EXACTLY what the intent was, but thought it made no sense as my immediate impression was seeing &quot;cwm&quot; as &quot;valley&quot; and then doing a double-take and re-reading it as a verb.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't a serious suggestion, but I apologize for the potentially offensive use, and I do assure you that the book itself will at least pass by an actual speaker of Cymraeg, rather than my poor attempts as an American of Welsh and Irish heritage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 08-27-2016, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T06:51:20-07:00","id":959211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/957123-favorite-pantheon?p=958594#post958594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently, absent any comments to the contrary, this name DID get by Neal and his team as is. He threw it out there as an offhand joke. Things as bad, and worse, have gotten by editors of White Wolf games in the past. Great chance to catch it now and kill it dead, dead, dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may be overthinking this. As the person likely to write the Welsh material and who did not make the initial joke, I can assure you that your concerns about the title of a published gaming supplement being passed by a quite attentive developer without question or consideration are misplaced.<br /> <br /> You are, however, welcome to question me about my background in the field.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T08:57:39-07:00","id":959286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geoffrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/957123-favorite-pantheon?p=959211#post959211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You may be overthinking this. As the person likely to write the Welsh material and who did not make the initial joke, I can assure you that your concerns about the title of a published gaming supplement being passed by a quite attentive developer without question or consideration are misplaced.<br /> <br /> You are, however, welcome to question me about my background in the field.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's NOT the issue. Things have gotten past developing teams in the past. E.g. Changeling stating that autistic people are Banal monsters who destroy creativity and joy by their mere presence. Which is only one of many examples. Instead of questioning my &quot;overthinking&quot;, you might, instead, be pleased that I pointed this out to you before it sailed through the development process with chuckles all around (which, again HAS happened numerous times). I didn't overthink a damn thing. It occurred to be immediately upon reading the statement. It reads as bad if you come off defensive about these things. You will get backed up by the cadre of posters that think that everything the developers do is just the greatest... but that's like trying to discuss sports with someone who believes their team can do no wrong. You're vetting your ideas in an echo chamber. <br /> <br /> I honestly don't have much concern about your credentials. To a point. It's not like you're putting forth you and the development team's version of the Welsh &quot;mythos&quot; such as it is in a scholarly journal, where such criticism is essential. But, then again, you are going to be MANY peoples' first point of contact with the somewhat obscure, difficult to access, often misunderstood and fairly thin (compared to other cultures) myths and legends. (Technically more the later). There is a certain level of responsibility in that that should be undertaken with due consideration. Consideration, I might add, that I see being taken elsewhere. I may not agree with all the specifics of the decisions being made, but they are perfectly good card tosses into a moving hat. <br /> <br /> I don't need or want a CV and a list of sources you're using. Anymore than I am going to provide such in return (which led to some posters accusing me of being a &quot;talking parrot with access to a keyboard&quot;, but, then again, they didn't offer their credentials either... ) (I think I remember that's actually against the policies of the board?) You could wade through Middle Age's Welsh text and try to troll Culwych &amp; Olwen to grab the least little things or you could riff off Evangeline Walton and Susan Cooper. Either way you could end up making a GREAT and playable Welsh pantheon that will give the players who want to splash around in it a ton of fun and, to those who knew nothing of the coolness of Welshness a taste of that flavor of magic. <br /> <br /> Also, thanks Neall for your replies to my concerns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T11:19:48-07:00","id":959344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/957123-favorite-pantheon?p=959286#post959286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of questioning my &quot;overthinking&quot;, you might, instead, be pleased that I pointed this out to you before it sailed through the development process with chuckles all around (which, again HAS happened numerous times). I didn't overthink a damn thing. It occurred to be immediately upon reading the statement. It reads as bad if you come off defensive about these things.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, thank you for pointing this out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T13:03:37-07:00","id":959391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geoffrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/957123-favorite-pantheon?p=959344#post959344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In that case, thank you for pointing this out.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome. And thanks again to Neall as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T13:33:33-07:00","id":959417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/957123-favorite-pantheon?p=958951#post958951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It wasn't a serious suggestion, but I apologize for the potentially offensive use, and I do assure you that the book itself will at least pass by an actual speaker of Cymraeg, rather than my poor attempts as an American of Welsh and Irish heritage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Genuine question, how is such a person verified to have a native command of the language?<br /> I'm just thinking of this as a Gaelic speaker, as I have encountered Anglophone Irish (i.e. don't speak Gaelic) people claiming to speak Gaelic to American companies resulting in crazy sentences making their way into books. I know Welsh has far more speakers than Irish, but still it's a general issue for minority languages, I've seen the same thing with Basque.<br /> <br /> I don't mean this in an antagonistic way, just an issue you may not be aware of and really it's very hard to get right, I mean large companies can still mess up English or Chinese translations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T15:41:40-07:00","id":959527,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit flabbergasted that there's all of this skepticism that No One Can Do Wales Right considering that Howard Ingham's treatment of Swansea in Changeling: the Lost was spectacular. That's the only version of OPP/WW doing Wales that I can think of.<br /> <br /> (Ingham is a sais like me, of course, but he is fluent in Welsh, his children are native speakers, and he has lived in Wales his entire adult life.)<br /> <br /> Maybe extend a bit of good faith, eh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1403-dymphna","name":"Dymphna","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T16:34:23-07:00","id":959563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dymphna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/957123-favorite-pantheon?p=959527#post959527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a bit flabbergasted that there's all of this skepticism that No One Can Do Wales Right considering that Howard Ingham's treatment of Swansea in Changeling: the Lost was spectacular. That's the only version of OPP/WW doing Wales that I can think of.<br /> <br /> (Ingham is a sais like me, of course, but he is fluent in Welsh, his children are native speakers, and he has lived in Wales his entire adult life.)<br /> <br /> Maybe extend a bit of good faith, eh?</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally didn't think Wales would be done wrong, just wondering how the correctness of the Welsh would be verified, no lack of faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T09:40:13-07:00","id":959868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/957123-favorite-pantheon?p=959563#post959563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally didn't think Wales would be done wrong, just wondering how the correctness of the Welsh would be verified, no lack of faith.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I genuinely don't want to sound defensive about this, because I know you're asking in good faith, but... I don't know, I can tell you the story of the three old Welshmen who kept referring to me as the Sais (or sometimes Americanwr, because they couldn't decide) and also didn't know that I understood them in the village where I lived? Or the man who asked me where I came from and said the word &quot;Canada&quot; in such a slow syllabic pronunciation that I still think he'd never said it before. All these years later, I remember his &quot;Ca-Na-Da. You're a long way from Ca-Na-Da.&quot;<br /> <br /> That said, here's a good story: I went to the shop one day\u2014there was only one, and it doubled as post office and &quot;place where we have a phone&quot;\u2014and heard this reply from the lady working there: &quot;You're looking for Mrs. Jones? We have a lot of people named Jones here. She's the daughter of Mair Jones? That doesn't help. Can you be more specific?&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd bought my milk-free chocolate at that point (I was living with a vegan), so didn't hear the rest, but I will always remember someone calling a Welsh village and asking for someone named &quot;Jones.&quot;<br /> <br /> Bonus: I can tell you about what I am absolutely sure was the only vegan Santaria devotee in Wales, along with a fellow who called himself &quot;Bunny&quot; and claimed to be an astral projectionist. &quot;I've never done it, of course, but I try.&quot;<br /> <br /> *edited to fix punctuation*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T11:52:47-07:00","id":959938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geoffrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/957123-favorite-pantheon?p=959868#post959868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I genuinely don't want to sound defensive about this, because I know you're asking in good faith, but... I don't know, I can tell you the story of the three old Welshmen who kept referring to me as the Sais (or sometimes Americanwr, because they couldn't decide) and also didn't know that I understood them in the village where I lived? Or the man who asked me where I came from and said the word &quot;Canada&quot; in such a slow syllabic pronunciation that I still think he'd never said it before. All these years later, I remember his &quot;Ca-Na-Da. You're a long way from Ca-Na-Da.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No need to worry about sounding defensive, you're entitled to defend yourself <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> and I've no real doubts about the quality of the Welsh, it's just an abstract question about the process. If you live in a Welsh speaking area that's more than enough (actually means more to me than an academic qualification, since it would require speaking it in a day-to-day manner).<br /> <br /> Truth told Welsh is in a better position than Irish and Basque in this regard, as there isn't a large body of non-natives speaking a constructed dialect influenced by their L1 (I know about Literary Welsh, but it isn't quite the same thing). Non-natives mostly learn from natives in Cambrophone areas, rather than other non-natives in Anglophone or Hispanophone areas.<br /> <br /> Also my favourite pantheon is Mesopotamian!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T12:13:26-07:00","id":959949,"title":"","content":"Orisha/Dev\u00e1","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T12:45:02-07:00","id":959967,"title":"","content":"I've pretty much fell in love in Celtic Mythology around the time I was a teenagers, and never stopped loving it since. Irish, especially, was my favorite, so it is hardy a wonder that the Tuatha are my favorite pantheon- although Welsh would come close, especially since I just love the language aesthetically. Among the many mythologies, the Mesopotamian took my the longest to open up to, but once I did I've really liked them (not like the Irish, but still)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T13:01:56-07:00","id":959975,"title":"","content":"1) Theoi<br /> 2) Egyptian/Norse/Celts<br /> 3) Chinese/Japanese","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T13:05:29-07:00","id":959976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/957123-favorite-pantheon?p=959975#post959975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Theoi<br /> 2) Egyptian/Norse/Celts<br /> 3) Chinese/Japanese</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait,the fellow named ACHILLES with the theoi simple in profile fic likes the theoi? SHOCK AND MOTHERFUCKING AWE,THAT'S THE SURPRISE OF THE YEAR.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T13:52:18-07:00","id":960003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/957123-favorite-pantheon?p=959976#post959976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait,the fellow named ACHILLES with the theoi simple in profile fic likes the theoi? SHOCK AND MOTHERFUCKING AWE,THAT'S THE SURPRISE OF THE YEAR.</div> </div> </div> </div> I KNOW!!. I guess being first generation Greek maaay have something to do with it. I also wrote up a Ragnarok style book 'fixing' the Greeks...but I'm not obsessed or anything. I can stop right after I finish the Titans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T22:50:53-07:00","id":960248,"title":"","content":"Don't suppose you have that Greek book available anywhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T23:06:42-07:00","id":960257,"title":"","content":"Based on the comment about Titans, I assume they're still working on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T01:34:59-07:00","id":960301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/957123-favorite-pantheon?p=960248#post960248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't suppose you have that Greek book available anywhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be interested in seeing it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T06:31:56-07:00","id":960396,"title":"","content":"Sure. PM me and I'll send it to you. Obvious warning I'm biased about the Theoi. So take from it what you will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T08:05:37-07:00","id":961061,"title":"","content":"I've always been kinda obsessed with religion and my family being Catholic, I got obsessed with Catholicism first. I guess I always wanted to be religious but something in my brain never really let me go from being a lover of a religion to a believer no matter how I tried. Mythology was my way to love more religions, I guess, so I like them for different things?<br /> <br /> Hero cults in Greek Mythology seem so powerful, and I like that Egyptian Gods are more Primal then many other religions, less personified. An obsession with proper conduct in Aztec mythos has a strange catharsis about it. I think my favorite if I had to pick is Vodoun? Symbolism made concretely physical, and its syncretic nature with Catholicism, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T09:07:03-07:00","id":961078,"title":"","content":"The problem with the Loa vis-a-vis is a lack of actual mythology in a game that's about mythology and not religion. <br /> <br /> For example: Remember that great story about the time the Baron Samedi captured Chango's <i>ti bon ange</i> and made him a zombie, so he could steal Agwe's favorite hat? And then Erzuli Freda used her seductive wiles to trick the zombie Chango into eating salt so that he was freed?<br /> <br /> You don't. Because we don't really have much in the way of such stories. That makes it more difficult to use the Loa in the same way one can use the mythologies of the Greeks, Irish, Norse, Aztecs and so on. That's why the move towards the Orisha is a good step. They have mythology galore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T09:44:32-07:00","id":961091,"title":"","content":"I find the best way there is to link the symbols. You don't really need stories, just a theme for the game. I mean the first game I heavily used the Loa was Werewolf where the idea of Spirits suited well and it helps players not immediately familiar with the mythology. I mean knowing some Veve is all you need to conjure up the story necessities that knowing myths would. Knowing the personalities and motifs of the gods works well AND it allows for more easy adaption to adding details and themes. Since the Loa are so vast and have many different connotations just talking about what color something is can give a ton of story strength and relate back to the pantheon. I mean people know the myth that Hephaestus caught his wife and her lover in his net, but their main go to is that he is a God of the Forge constantly making new things that the gods desire. Loa have that and more with their different &quot;personifications&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T11:48:08-07:00","id":961141,"title":"","content":"My personal favs are:<br /> <br /> 1. The Amatsukami<br /> 2. The Loa/Orishas<br /> 3. The Devas","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3714-mysteris","name":"Mysteris","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T13:36:57-07:00","id":961211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/957123-favorite-pantheon?p=961091#post961091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the best way there is to link the symbols. You don't really need stories, just a theme for the game. I mean the first game I heavily used the Loa was Werewolf where the idea of Spirits suited well and it helps players not immediately familiar with the mythology. I mean knowing some Veve is all you need to conjure up the story necessities that knowing myths would. Knowing the personalities and motifs of the gods works well AND it allows for more easy adaption to adding details and themes. Since the Loa are so vast and have many different connotations just talking about what color something is can give a ton of story strength and relate back to the pantheon. I mean people know the myth that Hephaestus caught his wife and her lover in his net, but their main go to is that he is a God of the Forge constantly making new things that the gods desire. Loa have that and more with their different &quot;personifications&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps. But that's like saying a character's stat block is a great way to describe them. It's <b><i>a</i></b> way to describe them, but it's ultimately flat and is going to take a lot of work to bring to life. And by stat block I mean JUST the crunchy number-y bits, no description block. No history write up. Particularly nothing that relates to character as a person relating to other persons, places and things. <br /> <br /> You hand me a sheet of paper with an artist's picture of the good Baron, his veve and a truncated write-up like a profile from a dating website, it's NOT the same as knowing all the stories about him from mythology. Actually, thinking about it, I'd LOVE to see Baron Samedi's e-Harmony dating profile. That would make him a person who wants things. This is more like just seeing the D&amp;D tagline (Name, Deity of?, Gender, Color, Animal, etc. in a table format.) and then just slopping all over the place with those really broad brushstrokes.<br /> <br /> Hephaestus's identity is the &quot;God of the Forge&quot; and that's how the players are going to connect with him? How does that make him different from Goibniu, Ogun, Volund, any other smith deity or, for that matter, a Norse dwarf? It's his relationship with his mother, his wife, her lover and his half-sister. It's the stuff he's made. It's his <i><b>stories</b></i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T14:09:53-07:00","id":961226,"title":"","content":"Personally my two big favorites are the Tuatha and the Aesir, in that order. They always just popped out as really cool for me which may be in part because, since there's an actual threat of death and defeat for both pantheons which makes me feel a lot more invested in the Gods and heroes as being relatable characters, as opposed to say the theoi who despite their having human flaws, I'm hard pressed to feel empathy for the Greek gods, though they are one of the pantheons I know best. <br /> <br /> And it does not hurt that they are so frickin bad @$$! They just seem so cool for me to read about, and it's not coincidental that so many metal bands choose to adopt the Norse mythology/Viking motifs. As well the idea of the gods as presented in the Irish pantheon actually seemingly be sort of diluted and weakened by the world until they devolve from deity to the fair folk or mortals. I am also just so hype for Scion 2, I've started going through all my books, despite knowing I can never find a group to play with. Anyways, that's my two cents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T13:45:58-07:00","id":961877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/957123-favorite-pantheon?p=961078#post961078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with the Loa vis-a-vis is a lack of actual mythology in a game that's about mythology and not religion.<br /> <br /> For example: Remember that great story about the time the Baron Samedi captured Chango's <i>ti bon ange</i> and made him a zombie, so he could steal Agwe's favorite hat? And then Erzuli Freda used her seductive wiles to trick the zombie Chango into eating salt so that he was freed?<br /> <br /> You don't. Because we don't really have much in the way of such stories. That makes it more difficult to use the Loa in the same way one can use the mythologies of the Greeks, Irish, Norse, Aztecs and so on. That's why the move towards the Orisha is a good step. They have mythology galore.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my favorite story of the loa. A Haitian priest told it to an American scholar who told it to me in 2008.<br /> <br /> When Jesus died and was laid in the tomb, two Haitian soldiers stood outside to guard the entrance. When God descended from Heaven to speak the magic words that brought Jesus back from the dead, the two soldiers eavesdropped and heard those words. They remembered them and passed them down from generation to generation until they reached this aforementioned priest. That is how he knows the procedure to bring a zombie back from the grave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T15:15:58-07:00","id":972153,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm, a difficult question. As an American, I am obviously more familiar with the Theoi and the Aesir by general rule. I'd have to say my favorite would be whichever pantheon can provide the most story potential. Which... I'm trying not to reflexively say the Aesir since that is what my current campaign is based on and where I've been devoting the brunt of much of my studying/research. But I don't want to say the Theoi because I'm so knowledgeable about that area of mythology as well. Maybe it's a tie between those two.<br /> <br /> From a game mechanic point of view, I'm all about having the best stats as opposed to being a magic-user, so it's Theoi all the way for me there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}